prompt.sdd.runner.comment:
The comment of this stage on the tracker goes in the field comment: sections (a text for each section below, with its heading, in this order) and technical.
{sections}
{technical}
Rules: the sections are read by people who do not read code (product, support, whoever opened the issue): say what the behavior is, not how it is built; file, function and line names go only in technical. Impersonal: no first person, and no person or agent as the subject; the subject is the system or the behavior. Complete in itself: no mention of the thread, the agents, the tools, the run, local paths or commands you ran; no raw logs; never a credential, token or personal contact, even if the issue has one. When the issue's own words are quoted, quote them in a block. Leave a section's text empty when it has nothing to say.

prompt.sdd.runner.comment.pr:
